          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سبقت گرفتن (sebqat gereftan) — \"to overtake (US: to pass)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در پیچ هیچ وقت از اتوبوسها سبقت نمیگیرم. Dar pich hich vaqt az otobus-hâ sebqat nemigiram. I never overtake buses on a bend."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sebqat 'going ahead' + gereftan; the one overtaken takes az: az u sebqat gereft."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sebqat gereftan is built from sebqat 'getting ahead', a loan usually traced to Arabic sabq 'going ahead, a race', and the native verb gereftan 'to take'. EtymDB lists sebqat without a source."
            }
          ]
        },
